# The build context is harness/, not harness/backend/.
#
# It has to be: app/resources.py resolves ``web/`` and ``model/`` by walking two parents up
# from app/, which is /srv in the image, so those two directories have to be copyable from
# the context. With a backend/-only context they were unreachable and the image served a
# 404 at / and /playground - the same failure package.py was hardened against for the
# desktop bundle, with no gate covering the container.
#
# Widening the context means these exclusions are load-bearing: without them the build
# ships the Swift sources, the UI-test virtualenv and node_modules to the daemon.
# Nothing here may exclude backend/, web/ or model/.
native
ui-tests
node_modules
workspaces
docs
reference
.tmp
outputs

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache

backend/.data
backend/tests
backend/.env
backend/build
backend/dist
backend/.dockerignore

*.log
